===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|non|*hánn}}, from {{inh|non|gmq-pro|*ᚺᚨᚾᚨᛉ|ts=hānaʀ}}, of uncertain origin. Perhaps a compound of {{m|gmq-pro|*he-|sc=Latn}} (corresponding to {{cog|en|he}}) and {{m|gmq-pro|*ānaʀ|sc=Latn}} (from {{der|non|gem-pro|*jainaz}}, corresponding to {{cog|got|𐌾𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃}}) or even directly from {{m|gmq-pro|*ānaʀ|sc=Latn}} with ''h-'' added due to influence from the demonstrative pronoun {{m|non|hinn}}, or else perhaps directly inherited from Proto-Indo-European and answering to {{cog|grc|κεῖνος}}.

The long vowel is preserved in the masculine dative ''hǫ́num'' and feminine nominative ''hǫ́n'', both affected by u-umlaut (Proto-Norse ''*hānumʀ'', ''*hānu'').

