#* {{quote-book|non-oen|year=980–1015|title={{w|sv:Östergötlands runinskrifter 68|Östergötland Runic Inscription 68}} (Ög68)|text=ᛋᚢᛁᚾᛅ × ᚴᛅᚱᚦᛁ × ᛒᚱᚢ × ᚦᚽᛋᛁ × ᚽᚠᛏᛁᛦ × ᚬᚢᛁᚾᛏ × ᛒᚱᚢᚦᚢᚱ × ᛋᛁᚾ × ᚼᛆᚾ × ᚢᛆᛋ × ᚢᚽᛋᛏᚽᛦ × ᛏᛅᚢᚦᚽᛦ × ᛁ × ᚢᚽᚱᚽᚴᛋ × '''(ᚴ)ᛅᛁ-ᛁ'''|tr=Svæina gærði bro þessi æftiʀ Øyvind, broður sinn. Hann vas vestr dauðr i Værings '''skæiði'''.|t=Sveina made this bridge in memory of Eyvindr, his brother. He died in the west on Væringr's '''ship'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|non-oen|year=11th c.|title={{w|Södermanland Runic Inscription 171}} (Sö171)|text=(ᛁ)ᚾᚴ(ᛁ)ᚠ(ᛅ)[ᛋ]ᛏᚱ ᛫ ᛚ[ᛁ](ᛏ) (ᚼ)(ᛅ)ᚴᚢ... ᛋᛏ(ᛅ)...ᚾ ᛫ ᚽᚠᛏᛁᛦ ᛫ ᛋᛁᚼᚢᛁᚦ ᛫ ᚠᛅᚦ-ᚱ ᛫ ᛋᛁ[ᚾ ᛫ ᚼᛅᚾ ᛫ ᚠᛁᛅᛚ ᛫ ᛁ ᚼ]ᚢᛚ(ᛘ)[ᚴᛅᚱᚦᛁ ᛫ '''ᛋᚴᛅᛁᚦᛅᛦ''' ᛫ ᚢᛁᛋᛁ ᛘᛁ]ᚦ ᛫ ᛋᚴᛁ...ᚱᛅ|tr=Ingifastr let haggv[a] stæ[i]n æftiʀ Sigvið, fað[u]r sinn. Hann fioll i Holmgarði, '''skæiðaʀ''' visi með ski[pa]ra.|t=Ingifastr had the stone cut in memory of Sigviðr, his father. He fell in Holmgarðr, the '''ship's''' leader with the seamen.}}

