tafl:
===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|non|tafla<g:f>|tabla<g:f>}}
* {{alt|non|*tafli<g:m>}}

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|non|gmw-pro|*tabulā}}, from {{der|non|la|tabula|t=a tablet; a board or plank}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|tæfl|t=game board; board game}}.

The term appears related to {{cog|cy|tawl||a throw; interruption}} in {{m|cy|tawlbwrdd||tafl game, gameboard|lit=tawl-board}}, which is also found in {{cog|gmq|-}} as {{cog|non|taflborð}}, {{cog|gmq-osw|taflbordh}}, {{m|gmq-osw|taffwellbord||game board}}. The double use of “board” ({{lit|tablet table}}) in the compound, suggests that the fore element refers to something different, akin to Welsh ''tawl''. Since ''tafl'' can also refer to a “move” in a board game, which may suggest an earlier intermixing with a verb root, cognate to {{cog|cy|tawl}}, such as {{cog|gem-pro|*tablōną||to grapple, fumble}} → {{cog|non|*tafla}} → i-umlaut {{m|non|tefla||to game}}, but also in {{cog|non|dafla}}, {{cog|no|tafla}}, {{m|no|tavla}}, {{cog|sv|taffla}}, {{m|sv|tavla||to dabble}}, frequentative of {{m|gem-pro|*tabōną||to tap, dab, grope, finger}}. Welsh ''tawl'' in the sense of “interuption” is further comparable to related {{m|gem-pro|*tabjaną||to interupt}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|n|tafls|tǫfl}}

# [[board]], [[table]], [[tablet]]
# a [[gameboard]]
#: {{syn|non|taflborð}}
