-tu:
===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|non|þú}}
* {{alt|non|-du|-ðu}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|non|pronouns|cat2=clitics}} {{tlb|non|enclitic}}

# {{non-gloss|enclitic form of {{m|non|þú}}}}
#* Haralds saga hins hárfagra 41.
#*: Nú tók'''tu''' svá við sem várr konungr vildi.
#* Lokasenna 24.
#*: En þik síða kóðu / Samseyju í / ok drap'''tu''' á vétt sem vǫlur / vitka líki / fór'''tu''' verþjóð yfir / ok hugða ek þat args aðal
#: {{suffixusex|non|skalt|skaltu|altsuf=þú|t1=shalt|t2=shalt thou}}
#: {{suffixusex|non|lát|láttu|altsuf=þú|t1=let (impr.)|t2=let (impr.)}}

====Usage notes====
For reasons related to syntax, as well as Old Norse often explicitly stating the subject of verbs in the imperative, the verb is often followed by the subject pronoun. For {{m|non|þú}}, this is when it may take on an enclitic form. This is not to say, however, that whenever ''þú'' comes after a verb, it will always take an enclitic form. It could well stay separate for the sake of emphasis.

Which one of the variants {{m|non|-du}}, {{m|non|-ðu}} and {{m|non|-tu}} to use, is decided by the same rules that decide which dental suffix to take in the type 1 weak verbs. This form is used after hard consonants.

====Descendants====
This feature is also present in modern Icelandic verb conjugation, with its imperative forms with appended personal pronouns (though only in the second person).

====See also====
* {{l|non|-k}}

